<title>UK: OFT invites comment on Rugby buying Boral.</title>
<headline>OFT invites comment on Rugby buying Boral.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK competition watchdog the Office of Fair Trading on Wednesday said it was examining whether the proposed acquisition of Boral (UK) Ltd by Rugby Group Plc qualified for further investigation under the Fair Trading Act.</p>
<p>If the OFI decides it does qualify, a further investigation will take place, with a view to advising the President of the Board of Trade Ian Lang on whether there should be a final referral to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission.</p>
<p>Rugby is a UK building company.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
